Shared .env syntax fixtures (fake values only). Each file defines TG_BOT_TOKEN (a Worker secret in
secrets.manifest and a REQUIRED_ENV key) and its FIRST line says what every parser must do:
  # expect-value: X   valid, and TG_BOT_TOKEN has the value X (empty X = counts as missing)
  # expect-invalid    must be rejected
Consumers: ingest/test_env_syntax.py (tg_check.parse_env), scripts/test-sync-secrets.sh and
scripts/test-check-local-prereqs.sh (the latter only sees present / missing / invalid).
The expectation line is a comment, so it does not affect parsing. A CRLF case is generated in the tests,
because the file tooling does not keep carriage returns.
